## Interface: 16001
## Title: PadleyUI (Forever probe)
## Notes: TEMPORARY - capability probe for the WoW Forever port. No skins load.
## Author: Padley
## Version: @project-version@
## X-PadleyUI-TOC: Forever
## OptionalDeps: Blizzard_DamageMeter, Blizzard_UIPanels_Game, BetterBags, Blizzard_ObjectiveTracker, Blizzard_TokenUI, Blizzard_Professions, Blizzard_ProfessionsBook, Blizzard_Collections, Blizzard_GroupFinder, Blizzard_EncounterJournal, Blizzard_WorldMap
## SavedVariables: PadleyUI_DB

# Fallback for the documented "_Forever" alias only. Not read on build 70338.
#
# Measured on Forever beta build 70338: the client (game type "camelot") reads
# PadleyUI_Camelot.toc. The documented "_Forever" alias was NOT honoured - with
# only PadleyUI_Forever.toc present the addon vanished from the addon list.
# Keep both files with distinct X-PadleyUI-TOC values; the probe records the
# one actually read as build.tocVariant.
#
# Retail (game type "standard") reads neither file and keeps using PadleyUI.toc.
# Do NOT add a _Mainline.toc: that family suffix would also be picked up by
# retail, ahead of the unsuffixed PadleyUI.toc.
#
# HAZARD: if no suffixed TOC matches the client's game type, WoW falls back to
# the unsuffixed PadleyUI.toc and loads every retail skin into Forever.
#
# OptionalDeps mirror PadleyUI.toc so the probe sees the same load order the
# retail skins would.
#
# Core\Fonts.lua is deliberately excluded: it is not inert (it rewrites
# STANDARD_TEXT_FONT and SetFont()s every global Font object at load).

Core\Constants.lua

# TEMPORARY diagnostic — /puiforever, writes PadleyUI_DB.foreverProbe.
Debug\ForeverProbe.lua
